OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G5/9
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Northern Ireland security minister Mr
OL,6, John Cope has denied collusion between
OL,7, the security forces and terrorists.
OL,9,FSpeaking to journalists, he dismissed
OL,10,Fallegations by SDLP deputy leader Mr
OL,11,FSeamus Mallon that there was a policy
OL,12,Fof collusion.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FMr Mallon had implied that confidential
OL,15,Fdocuments listing IRA suspects did not
OL,16,Ffind their way into the hands of
OL,17,Floyalist paramilitaries by accident.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FThe security forces are investigating
OL,20,Fthe disappearance of the confidential
OL,21,Fdocuments.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 21-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,180,120,250,0,100
