OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G8/9
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, A United States court has awarded
OL,6, temporary custody of seven frozen
OL,7, embryos to a divorced woman who wants
OL,8, to have a test-tube baby.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FMiss Mary Sue Davis argued that the
OL,11,Fembryos, fertilised with sperm from her
OL,12,Fformer husband, were her best chance of
OL,13,Fbecoming a mother.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FHer ex-husband fought her claim for
OL,16,Fcustody, saying he did not want to
OL,17,Fbecome a father against his will.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FJudge W Dale Young said final custody
OL,20,Fwill be decided if one of the embryos
OL,21,Fresults in a birth.
OL,23,T]CFrom 21-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
